<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $83.9 mln Nov 4.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $83.9 mln Nov 4.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $83.9 million surplus on November 4 according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 4</p>
<p>Exports: $168.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $228 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $290.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $147.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $83.9 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $401.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $385.7 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $594.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $380.6 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $229.5 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
